@@ -40,6 +40,9 @@ Names are not identifiers (124 duplicated EA names): every item carries club, na
 ## getPlayer behaviour decided in Step 4.3
 Id: `^ea:(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,8})$` only. Malformed (incl. `p:<uuid>`, wrong case, leading zeros, non-ASCII digits, trailing characters) -> 400 `INVALID_PLAYER_ID` with `instance` null (the rejected value is not reflected); unknown well-formed id -> 404. `provenance` = one entry per contributing source in registry order (see `ARCHITECTURE_API.md` 6.2).
 
+## getPlayerMarketValue behaviour decided in Step 4.4
+Same id grammar and errors as `getPlayer`. Source market value only (never EA value or model estimate; no derived fields). EA-only -> `200 NOT_MATCHED`, empty `points`, `latest` null. Canonical without rows -> `200 NO_SOURCE_DATA`. `points` sorted `valuation_date` ASC then `dataset_version` ASC; `latest` = last point (highest date, ties -> newest dataset_version) = the value `getPlayer` shows. Rows with the same `(valuation_date, source, dataset_version)` collapse to the latest import. A NULL source column omits `source` from the point and gives `data_origin` UNKNOWN. `contains_sample_data` = a shown point is SAMPLE_FIXTURE. The contract itself is unchanged (still 0.4.0-draft): the implementation conforms to it.
+
 ## Error model
 `application/problem+json` (RFC 9457): `type,title,status,code,detail,instance,errors[]`.
 Codes: `INVALID_PARAMETER`(400) `INVALID_PLAYER_ID`(400) `PLAYER_NOT_FOUND`(404, unknown id only) `DATA_UNAVAILABLE`(503) `INTERNAL_ERROR`(500). No SQL, paths or stack traces in `detail`.
